{"author":{"id":"337a442880d7106d509ff84f2f7fef51acce8bce88b081d4f4c3f0298b7e7941"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1791828028,"nonce":"Dt+/PgxOuqplgquppNml4KUGxZM=","message":"Decision: db.connect now returns a sqlite3.Connection subclass carrying an RLock; FetchContext and the runner hold it for every statement while the fan-out runs, and a connection without it (plain sqlite3.connect) forces a serial run. List-stage stubs are buffered per source and written on the run thread in plan order. Reason: one writer, no statement landing in another thread's transaction, and job ids identical to a serial run. Cost: a source finished early waits in memory for earlier ones; a crash loses those unwritten stubs, which the next run refetches (mostly 304s).","files":null}]}